sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0244 task, DECISIONS R1 (record-only change starts no run), R2, R4. Same shape as tool.install.
  %% status: reviewed
  %% command: tool:remove
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant N as Target Node<br/>reached over ssh
  CLI->>GW: tool:remove 31<br/>Tool id · --yes
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit tool:remove 31 --yes`
  %%> - syntax: `<tool> [--yes]`
  %%> Input:
  %%> - the Tool's id, as `tool:list --node=ID` shows it
  %%> Confirmation:
  %%> - without `--yes`, the CLI first asks "Remove Tool ripgrep (apt on Node #12) by uninstalling it and deleting its record?"; the default is No
  %%> - without a terminal, or with `--json`, `--yes` is required
  Note over GW: Validate, lock the manager<br/>task #5135 · ripgrep on Node 12
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - your Node has an access grant to Node 12
  %%> - Tool 31 exists
  %%> - no other change runs for this Tool Manager on Node 12; the Gateway holds one lock per Node and Tool Manager
  %%> Decides:
  %%> - whether the package must leave the Node, or only the record goes
  alt package belongs to a role
    Note over GW: Delete only the record<br/>R1: no run, package stays
    %%> When:
    %%> - the package is owned by a Node role, for example a PHP extension such as `php8.5-xml`
    %%> Result:
    %%> - Tool 31's record is deleted
    %%> - the package stays installed, because the role still needs it
    %%> - no Swamp run starts (R1)
    GW-->>CLI: Tool removed<br/>package kept for the role
    %%> What you get:
    %%> - the final result at once; there is nothing to follow
  else Orbit installed it
    GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-tool-remove
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - starts one Swamp run on serve (Node 209)
    %%> Inputs:
    %%> - the package, Tool Manager, and whether its apt source is still used by another Tool
    %%> - Node 12's address and SSH host keys; the SSH identity comes from the `swamp` role
    GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task #5135
    %%> What you get:
    %%> - the task number, at once
    %%> Next:
    %%> - the CLI follows the task with `operation:show`
    SW->>N: Plan the removal<br/>e.g. apt-get --simulate remove
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - asks the Tool Manager what removing the package would also remove
    %%> Refuses:
    %%> - a plan that removes any other package; then the run stops here and nothing changes
    %%> Per Tool Manager:
    %%> - `apt`: `apt-get --simulate remove`; the plan may contain only this package
    %%> - `brew`: refuses when another formula still depends on it
    %%> - `brew-cask`: checks the cask is safe to uninstall
    %%> - `composer`, `vp`: no plan needed; global packages have no system dependents
    SW->>N: Remove the package<br/>e.g. dpkg --remove
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - removes exactly this package, so dependency changes can't pull in more removals
    %%> - no purge, no autoremove
    %%> Per Tool Manager:
    %%> - `apt`: `dpkg --remove`, as root
    %%> - `brew`, `brew-cask`: `brew uninstall`, as the Node's account
    %%> - `composer`, `vp`: removes the global package, as the Node's managed user
    %%> Busy apt lock:
    %%> - it waits for the lock within the run's time budget, then fails
    SW->>N: Check it is gone<br/>package query
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - asks the Tool Manager again; the package must be absent
    %%> Why:
    %%> - the Tool only counts as removed when the Node shows it
    alt package is gone
      N-->>SW: ripgrep absent
      %%> Returns:
      %%> - the check passed
      opt last Tool from that apt source
        SW->>N: Remove the apt source<br/>no Tool uses it anymore
        %%> When:
        %%> - only when this was the last Tool installed from a signed apt repository
        %%> What it does:
        %%> - removes the apt source and its signing key from the Node
        %%> If it fails:
        %%> - the removal still succeeds; the package is already gone
        %%> - the unused apt source stays recorded, and the next `tool:remove` or `tool:install` from it cleans it up
      end
      SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
      %%> How the Gateway learns it:
      %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event; Swamp never calls the Gateway
      Note over GW: Delete the Tool<br/>record gone · task succeeded
      %%> Result:
      %%> - Tool 31's record is deleted
      %%> - an apt repository record is deleted when its source was removed; otherwise it stays recorded for a later cleanup
      %%> - task #5135 succeeds
    else a step fails
      N--xSW: plan too wide or exit ≠ 0
      %%> When:
      %%> - the plan would remove other packages, the removal fails, or the package is still there
      SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
      %%> The Gateway reads:
      %%> - which step failed and its error code
      Note over GW: Mark the Tool failed<br/>keeps 14.1.1 · rerun after a fix
      %%> Result:
      %%> - Tool 31 stays, marked failed, with its recorded version
      %%> - task #5135 fails
      %%> Retry:
      %%> - run the same command again
    end
    loop every 2 s until terminal
      CLI->>GW: operation:show #5135
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - asks for the task's status every 2 seconds until it has ended
      GW-->>CLI: status + result
      %%> Returns:
      %%> - the current status, and the result once the task has ended
    end
  end
